#text("Derived and qualified 2026-11-09, T-1968. The signed baby denominator norm can be evaluated by two polynomial evaluations and fourth powers, with no field inverse. The contract is qualified independently of the complete first-response pipeline. All scientific results remain unverified producer evidence. [pcc:unverified]")
#parbreak()
#text("Proof. Let H_G(Z)=product_j(Z-x(jG)), with distinct baby roots, and beta(x(jG))=x(jQ). Define H_Q(Z)=product_j(Z-x(jQ)). For giant inputs A,B put D=(x(A)-Z)^2*(x(B)-beta(Z))^2 in K[Z]/H_G. Evaluating D^2 at every root gives Norm(D^2)=product_j(x(A)-x(jG))^4*(x(B)-x(jQ))^4=H_G(x(A))^4*H_Q(x(B))^4. The nonrational-shift guards from Round63 ensure every factor is nonzero. This is standard norm multiplicativity applied to the retained signed input; it does not require constructing D^2 or computing its resultant. [pcc:unverified]")
#parbreak()
#text("Frozen panel. All 11,382 full baby blocks from the unchanged Round63/64 query inputs match the field-resultant denominator value. Polynomial preparation, target H_Q setup and each isolated evaluator have separate counters. The evaluation path records 147,138 K multiplications and zero inversions, versus 2,171,092 multiplications and 67,255 inversions in the resultant path. Target H_Q construction costs 496 additional multiplications. The degree-one panel uses 2,800 evaluation multiplications versus 1,200 in the reference; all panels remain in the record. No timings or complete-evaluator speedup are inferred. [pcc:unverified]")
#parbreak()
#text("Primary P192 checks. The 72 prescribed degree-four denominator norms on the existing publicQ,mu_G,relation_lambda_G all match. The two paths use 1,080/0 and 2,808/360 explicit K multiplication/inverse calls respectively. These counters exclude inverse internals and are not combined with the small-field model. Polynomial inputs and curve points are explicitly prepared; no full P192 response or arbitrary-input decoder is executed. [pcc:unverified]")
